diff --git a/docs/BACKENDS.md b/docs/BACKENDS.md
index 6ccbc5c3..157e6e05 100644
--- a/docs/BACKENDS.md
+++ b/docs/BACKENDS.md
@@ -184,6 +184,32 @@ the previous request's high water. Parked sessions retain their Host-backed hist
 steps with 1024 rows of lookahead. `poly_elastic_test MODEL.gguf --kv-reclaim-test` checks accepted KV, recurrent
 state, statistics and restored-session logits across immediate reclamation.
 
+On Windows CUDA, `--elastic-experts-headroom` additionally opts into bounded steady-decode borrowing and implies
+`--elastic-experts`. After 128 decode calls it can use the reserve down to 128 MiB; after 256 calls it can exceed
+the worker's DXGI local budget by at most 128 MiB, while keeping at least 512 MiB physically free according to
+NVML. A configured reserve above 256 MiB increases these margins. DXGI and NVML must identify the same CUDA
+adapter. The worker repays any signed budget excess and restores the full configured reserve before prefill
+or KV expansion. Missing telemetry or shared-memory growth above the sampled baseline by 16 MiB disables
+borrowing for the worker's remaining lifetime; ordinary elastic behavior continues. An allocation failure
+above budget gives back a 64 MiB piece and lowers the borrowing ceiling for the worker lifetime; a failure
+without enough borrowed memory to retreat disables borrowing. The failed ceiling is not repeatedly retried.
+External physical pressure shrinks the cache. Unsupported platforms use ordinary elastic behavior.
+
+Use `["--elastic-experts", "--elastic-experts-headroom"]` in the console's native arguments; remove the second
+flag to compare ordinary elastic allocation. INFO also exposes physical free memory, DXGI budget/local/shared
+usage, headroom state and mapped KV rows/MiB. `poly_elastic_test MODEL.gguf --headroom-test` exercises real decode
+growth, prefill/KV repayment and injected pressure/allocation/telemetry/shared-memory failures. Borrowing beyond
+the Windows budget is opt-in; qualify decode performance on the target machine before enabling it.
+
+`--elastic-headroom-mib N` controls the above-budget ceiling (default 128, range 0..1024 MiB), and
+`--elastic-physical-reserve-mib N` controls the physical-free floor (default 512, range 256..4096 MiB).
+Both require the headroom switch to take effect. For an aggressive target use native arguments
+`["--elastic-experts-headroom", "--elastic-headroom-mib", "512", "--elastic-physical-reserve-mib", "256"]`.
+These are ceilings/targets, not promised allocations: WDDM can reject mappings before the physical floor.
+INFO reports requested and learned ceilings, the physical reserve and allocation backoff count.
+`poly_elastic_test MODEL.gguf --aggressive-test` checks this configuration and verifies that a learned ceiling
+is retained across later decode ticks, alongside the existing repayment and accepted-state checks.
+
 ## How a backend works
 
 There are two levels.
